  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xEDFA" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Throttled</title>
    <description>Exact 1ME3B. Address 0x173D6; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 4 duration target of the VVEL resolver: the throttled pair. Interpolated by engine speed and scaled by 0.05; FUN_00063534 publishes the curve value or a stepped approach to it from ROM16[0x94A6] * 0.05 = 50.0. Exact 1ME3B target-native table at 0x173d6 bound to accessor 0x63534 through literal 0x637c8, accessor 0x7448c through literal 0x74fdc, accessor 0x7448c through literal 0x7525c. Read by FUN_00063534 at callsite 0x63570 through the 16-point uint16 leaf 0x2AF88 and by FUN_0007448C at 0x74EEC, 0x7510C, and 0x751E4 with the same axis; the resolver FUN_00062FAC calls FUN_00063534 after the hot-intake idle pair. The 0.05 factor is the float literal 0x3D4CCCCC at 0x637D0. FUN_00063534 keeps the scaled curve value at 0xFFFEF458 and publishes the pair 3 duration slot 0xFFFEF460 as that value or as 50.0 plus an offset that steps by ROM16[0x9384] * 0.001 = 0.05 toward the curve value within +/-50.0; the delay helper FUN_0002861E gates the offset with a time from the byte curve 0x0001457A over axis 0x00014582. The JK78C and 1ND0A resolvers store the curve value directly. Stock bytes are identical to JK78C 0x00016D14.</description>
