    <title>Map 1 - Ignition Timing Surface - VVEL State Codes 2 and 8</title>
    <description>Exact 1ME3B. Address 0xA344; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Ignition surface for state codes 2 and 8, VVEL modes 5 and 15, of the mode-selected half of the ignition coordinator FUN_000797CC, the only half this coordinator carries. Stock ROM8[0x8A7D] = 0x1C (bit 3 set) selects the surface by the state-code byte 0xFFFEB826, which the mapper FUN_00050310 derives from the VVEL mode: mode 5 gives code 2, mode 3 code 3, mode 10 code 4, mode 12 code 5, mode 13 code 6, mode 14 code 7, mode 15 code 8, and every other mode code 1. The coordinator takes the low seven bits of the lookup and crossfades the previous and current state values by the progress word 0xFFFEB824, where 0x8000 is 1.0. Common-definition Map 1 uses the canonical stock storage. This view edits mask 0x7F and preserves the other bits in each cell. Exact 1ME3B target-native table at 0xa344 bound to accessor 0x797cc through literal 0x79cb0, accessor 0x797cc through literal 0x79e20. Byte-identical to the JK78C hot-coolant surface 0xA10A. The literal words 0x79424, 0x796F0, 0x799A0 hold the same address; the structure export recovers no instruction that reads them.</description>
