    <title>Map 1 - Ignition Timing Surface - VVEL State Code 1</title>
    <description>Exact 1ME3B. Address 0xA444; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Ignition surface for state code 1, every VVEL mode outside 3, 5, 10, 12, 13, 14, and 15, of the mode-selected half of the ignition coordinator FUN_000797CC, the only half this coordinator carries. Stock ROM8[0x8A7D] = 0x1C (bit 3 set) selects the surface by the state-code byte 0xFFFEB826, which the mapper FUN_00050310 derives from the VVEL mode: mode 5 gives code 2, mode 3 code 3, mode 10 code 4, mode 12 code 5, mode 13 code 6, mode 14 code 7, mode 15 code 8, and every other mode code 1. The coordinator takes the low seven bits of the lookup and crossfades the previous and current state values by the progress word 0xFFFEB824, where 0x8000 is 1.0. Common-definition Map 1 uses the canonical stock storage. This view edits mask 0x7F and preserves the other bits in each cell. Exact 1ME3B target-native table at 0xa444 bound to accessor 0x797cc through literal 0x79ca8. Byte-identical to the JK78C cold-coolant surface 0xA20A. The literal words 0x7941C, 0x7971C hold the same address; the structure export recovers no instruction that reads them.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="13" />
