  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x225A" flags="0x0">
    <title>Map 2 - Timing-State Addend - Warm DFCO Transition - Default</title>
    <description>Exact 1ME3B. Address 0x13D0A0; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Warm DFCO-transition eight-point timing-state addend. FUN 0004afdc selects it only when ffff244f.bit2 is clear, warm latch ffff41de.bit5 is set, upstream DFCO mode ffff2458.bit5 is set, and transition timer ffff2590 is nonzero. Target variant: Default. Common-definition Map 2 storage is projected from 0x13A26. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. The warm latch sets at raw coolant 110 and remains set down to raw 106, corresponding to 60 and 56 deg C under the exact diagnostic conversion. While ffff2458.bit5 is clear, ffff2590 reloads to 85; once the bit is set, the periodic scheduler decrements it. Selection therefore lasts for at most 85 scheduler counts, or 870.4 ms at the target-measured 10.24 ms period. A2L homology identifies the historical Idle Ignition Timing name. The alternate compositor branch of 0004bdc2 forms ffff1830=clamp_s8(ffff1a7d+ffff23ee-ffff23c5-64) at 0004be82 and shares the ffff2404 -&gt; ffff2378 -&gt; ffff12d6 -&gt; ffff11da -&gt; ffff11d4 chain of coefficient 1 with the low-seven surfaces, and J1979 PID 0x0E publishes ffff11d4 as A/2-64 degBTDC, so one count of this map is one crank degree of the declared coordinate. Index: implicit eight-point axis over ffff11b2 with saturation at element 7. Result disposition: writes (RAM ffff1511, site 0004b0d0). Definition address projected from JK08A 0001219e through JK08A-1ME3B.definition-addresses.csv: the target coordinator 0007323e reads the exact table at ordinal 120 on the default arm and 00013a2e at ordinal 154 on the alternate arm exactly as 1ND0A 0006f37a reads 00013c1a and 00013c22. Static diagnostic context: IGN TIMING [candidate, homologous_vq35hr, via map evidence: writes].</description>
