  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x8F61" flags="0x0">
    <title>Map 3 - Ignition Timing Surface - VVEL State Codes 6 and 7</title>
    <description>Exact 1ME3B. Address 0x13E4C0; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Ignition surface for state codes 6 and 7, VVEL modes 13 and 14, of the mode-selected half of the ignition coordinator FUN_000797CC, the only half this coordinator carries. Stock ROM8[0x8A7D] = 0x1C (bit 3 set) selects the surface by the state-code byte 0xFFFEB826, which the mapper FUN_00050310 derives from the VVEL mode: mode 5 gives code 2, mode 3 code 3, mode 10 code 4, mode 12 code 5, mode 13 code 6, mode 14 code 7, mode 15 code 8, and every other mode code 1. The coordinator takes the low seven bits of the lookup and crossfades the previous and current state values by the progress word 0xFFFEB824, where 0x8000 is 1.0. Common-definition Map 3 storage is projected from 0xA604. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. This view edits mask 0x7F and preserves the other bits in each cell. Exact 1ME3B target-native table at 0xa604 bound to accessor 0x797cc through literal 0x799cc. Byte-identical to the 1ND0A surface 0xA6D0. The 8x8 lookup 0x000293D8 serves the four state-code surfaces of this coordinator. The literal words 0x79400 hold the same address; the structure export recovers no instruction that reads them.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="13" />
