  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x76F6" flags="0x0">
    <title>Map 5 - Fuel Compensation - Main - Alternate</title>
    <description>Exact 1ME3B. Address 0x13C000; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Alternate multiplicative fuel correction with raw 128 = 100% as neutral. It shares both coordinates, both axes, and the interpolator of the projected default surface 0x0000A0F4, and the state selector in FUN_000486E0 reads it in place of that surface for state code 2. Common-definition Map 5 storage is projected from 0xA1F4. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. Exact 1ME3B target-native table at 0xa1f4 bound to accessor 0x3357c through literal 0x33ed8, accessor 0x486e0 through literal 0x48b7c. Read by FUN_0003357C at callsite 0x33CEC and by FUN_000486E0 at 0x48A10 through the 16x16 uint8 leaf 0x298B4, in each accessor directly after the default surface 0x0000A0F4 with the same coordinates and the same axis pair 0x00013D06 and 0x00013D26, so neither surface carries an engine-bank identity. Both accessors store the default result in the channel byte 0xFFFE8ED6, this surface in 0xFFFE8ED7, and the curve 0x00013CF6 over axis 0x00013D16 in 0xFFFE8ED5. FUN_0003357C initializes the output byte 0xFFFE8ED4 and the held byte 0xFFFE8ED8 with the default channel. FUN_000486E0 selects a channel by a state code, where code 2 selects this surface, code 8 selects the curve, and every other code selects the default surface. It publishes in 0xFFFE8ED4 the crossfade of the channel of state byte 0xFFFEB822, weighted by the word 0xFFFEB820, against the channel of state byte 0xFFFEB850, or against the held output while the transition flag 0xFFFEBA3A.bit0 is set; the literal 0x8000 at 0x48B90 is weight 1.0. The call pair reproduces the 1ND0A accessors FUN_00030810 and FUN_00044F1C. Thirteen of the 256 stock cells differ from the JK78C surface 0x00009FBA.</description>
